/* ── The dashboard parts: action tiles, status rows, the facet list, the heat grid, the matrix, the bar in a cell, the
   week agenda and the run timeline [kpadopt2] ──
   Blueprint's own (themes/blueprint/CHARACTER.md): a tile is a part on the sheet, no fill and no frame, standing on the
   graticule's two axes (G7); pointing sets the amber witness lines at its two ends (G8); a press takes the dimension,
   an amber line across its foot with a slash at each end, and the part's ground never changes (G14); a failure is
   flagged, the filled triangle in the tone's ink before the title (G13); the lettering names (mono capitals sloped 15
   degrees), the sans speaks (G15); a waiting count is a section being hatched (G10); what runs is the chain line
   feeding along its dimension line (G11). Every stroke on the plotter's feed. */
